// LEC-005 (D25): a perfectly ordinary program that calls one generic function on
// 70 DIFFERENT types must compile and run. Before this milestone the monomorphizer
// capped the TOTAL number of instantiations it drained at
// Monomorphize::kMaxInstantiationDepth (64) -- named a depth, measuring a count --
// so the 65th independent `ident<S65>` was rejected with a bogus E079 whose
// "chain" was a dump of the whole instantiation cache. The cap now measures the
// real request chain (InstantiationRequest::Parent): 70 siblings are chains of
// length 1.
// EXPECT-NO-DIAG: E079
// EXPECT-NO-DIAG: instantiation depth exceeded
// (Generated: 70 one-field structs and one ident<S> call each; edit by hand, not by
// regenerating, if you change it.)
